    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Gordon Hughes Estate Agents are delighted to present this attractive four bedroomed semi-detached home, extending to approx. 130sqm, ideally positioned within the popular and mature Foxlodge development. \n\nThe property presents an appealing red & grey brick façade. The generous cobblelock driveway provides ample off-street parking, while mature planting and established greenery provides a good degree of privacy and enhances the property's kerb appeal. Internally the home offers well-proportioned and versatile accommodation, making it ideally suited to modern family living. With four bedrooms and three bathrooms, there is excellent space for a growing family or those working from home. \n\nTo the rear of the property lies a private, south facing, mature garden featuring a generous lawn bordered by an abundance of mature hedging and trees creating a wonderful sense of privacy and seclusion. There is also a useful garden shed, providing additional storage. A pathway rung along the rear and to the side of the property where an extremely large side access lies. \n\nFoxlodge Manor is a well-established and popular development located in the thriving village of Ratoath, Co. Meath. The development is characterised by attractive, traditionally styled homes, generous landscaped areas and mature planting creating a pleasant residential environment. Residents enjoy the convenience of being close to an excellent selection of local amenities, including shops, cafes, restaurants, schools, sporting facilities and public transport links. Foxlodge Manor also benefits from excellent access to the M2 & M3 motorway networks, providing convenient connectivity to Dublin and surrounding areas. \n\nViewing is highly recommended!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall 3.32m x 5.19m \nA spacious welcome to this family home fitted with coving, wide plank laminate flooring and alarm panel. Also hosts Guest WC 2.14m x 1.36m which is fitted with wc and whb. \n\nLivingroom 3.36m x 5.83m\nSpacious living room, located to the front of the property and with feature bay window. Fitted with laminate flooring, coving and central fireplace with gas inset. \n\nFamily room/Office 2.76m x 2.69m \nAlso located to the front of the property and suitable for a host of uses fitted with laminate flooring. \n \nOpen Plan Kitchen/Diner \nA great space, spanning the entire width of the rear of the property. The entire space is fitted with tiled flooring. The kitchen area 3.46m x 2.59m is fitted with wall and floor units, wooden effect worktops and tiled splashback. All appliances are being included in the sale. The dining section 4.43m x 3.35m has sliding patio doors which lead out to the rear garden. \n\nUtility 1.81m x 1.88m Located just off the kitchen, fitted with tiled floor and door leading out to the rear garden. \n\nLanding 2.33m x 2.58m \nA generous landing which hosts hot-press and also provides access to the attic. \n\nMaster Bedroom 4.52m x 3.78m \nLocated to the front of the property with wooden flooring and built in wardrobes. \n\nEn-Suite 2.35m x 1.04m \nFitted with wc, whb and pump shower. \n\nBedroom 2 3.21m x 3.56m \nLocated to the rear of the property a generous double bedroom. \n\nBedroom 3 3.27m x 2.78m \nAnother generous bedroom, which is located to the front of the property and is fitted with built in wardrobes. \n\nBedroom 4 2.76m x 2.51m \nLocated to the rear of the property. \n\nBathroom 2.09m x 2.43m \nA generous family bathroom which is fully tiled and fitted with wc, whb and bath with shower attachment."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Attractive four bedroomed, semi-detached home extending to c. 130sqm.\nWell-proportioned and versatile accommodation. \nSouth facing rear garden. \nNot overlooked to the front or rear. \nNicely positioned overlooking a large green, on a row of just four homes! \nLarger than normal side access. \nAttic suitable for conversion (subject to necessary permission). Attic currently floored. \nServices: Gas fired central heating, mains water and mains sewage. \nBER:B. BER Number: 119784395\nBuilt c. 2005.\nSituated in a mature, well-established development."
      },
